Article 5 When a case is entrusted for enforcement, the entrusting court shall provide the following materials:
(1) a letter of entrusted enforcement;
(2) the application for enforcement and the approval form for the entrusted enforcement case;
(3) a copy of the effective legal instrument on the basis of which enforcement is carried out;
(4) materials or explanations concerning the case, including investigation materials showing that there is no property within its jurisdiction, the status of property preservation, the property status of the person subject to enforcement, and the performance status of the effective legal instrument;
(5) the address and contact telephone number of the applicant for enforcement;
(6) copies of the identity document or business license of the person subject to enforcement, as well as the address and contact telephone number;
(7) the enforcement officer of the entrusting court and the contact telephone number; and
(8) other necessary case materials.

Article 13 The Higher People's Court shall exercise unified management and coordination over entrusted enforcement and cross-locality enforcement within its jurisdiction, and shall perform the following duties:
(1) uniformly managing entrusted and受托 enforcement cases across provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government;
(2) guiding, inspecting, and supervising the enforcement of受托 cases within its jurisdiction;
(3) coordinating disputed cases involving entrusted and受托 enforcement across provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government within its jurisdiction;
(4) handling approval matters for relevant cases requiring enforcement in different localities;
(5) putting forward guiding opinions on the handling of relevant issues in entrusted and受托 enforcement cases submitted by lower courts; and
(6) handling other matters involving entrusted enforcement work.
